            type: "example",
            title: "A Thimble That Changes Everything",
            content: "Want to feel how potent these messengers really are? Look at real numbers from medicine and daily life:\n\n• **Levothyroxine**, the synthetic thyroid hormone taken by millions, is dosed in **micrograms** — a typical tablet is 75 or 100 mcg, less than the weight of a grain of salt. Yet getting that dose wrong by a fraction can mean months of exhaustion or a racing heart.\n\n• When something startles you, your adrenals release **adrenaline** measured in nanograms — and within seconds your heart rate can nearly double, pupils dilate, and blood reroutes to your muscles.\n\n• The **estradiol** difference between feeling sharp and feeling foggy during perimenopause can be a swing of mere **picograms per milliliter** of blood.\n\nThis is why 'it's all in your head' is such a costly dismissal. A signal too small for any home scale to weigh can rewrite your energy, your appetite, and your mood. And it's why measuring these signals — with proper labs, at the right time of day — matters so much later in this book.",
