            content: "Every few minutes, your body answers one question: **store fuel, or release it?**\n\nGet the answer right, and you have steady energy, a clear head, and a metabolism that quietly does its job. Get it wrong — chronically — and you're on a conveyor belt toward the condition that affects more than 1 in 3 American adults before they ever hear the word 'diabetes.'\n\nTwo hormones from your pancreas make this call: **insulin**, the storage signal, and **glucagon**, the release signal. They are the fuel switches of your entire metabolism — and here's the part almost nobody is told: the switch can start sticking **10 or more years** before a diabetes diagnosis, while every routine glucose test still comes back 'normal.'\n\nThe good news? Few systems in your body respond faster to the right moves. A single walk after dinner changes this system today. Let's learn how the switches work — and how to keep yours flipping freely.",
