            content: "Pull the lesson together:\n\n• **Insulin stores, glucagon releases** — together they defend the single teaspoon of glucose in your blood, around the clock\n• **Insulin resistance** develops silently over **10+ years** while glucose tests stay normal — the pancreas compensates by shouting\n• **Muscle handles ~80%** of insulin-driven glucose disposal, and contraction bypasses insulin entirely — movement is direct medicine\n• **GLP-1**, your gut's own incretin, is the template for the blockbuster drugs — and it responds to protein, fiber, and meal order\n• **Every hormone in this book routes through insulin**: cortisol raises the glucose insulin must handle, thyroid sets the burn rate, estrogen and testosterone shape sensitivity and the muscle sink, sleep guards it all\n\nThe deepest reframe: insulin resistance is not a verdict — the Diabetes Prevention Program proved a **58% reduction** in progression with lifestyle alone. The decade of silence is a decade of leverage.\n\n**Next lesson**: the hormone that pushes hardest against insulin — **cortisol**, the stress currency. You'll learn why your worst blood-sugar days are often your most stressful ones, why 'adrenal fatigue' isn't what the internet says it is, and how to spend your stress currency instead of being spent by it.",
