            content: "Ever notice how you sometimes wake up moments before your alarm rings? That's not luck. That's **cortisol** — your body's stress currency — being spent exactly on schedule.\n\nAbout an hour before you wake, your adrenal glands begin ramping up cortisol. Roughly **30 minutes after your eyes open**, it surges to its daily peak — a phenomenon scientists call the **cortisol awakening response**. It mobilizes glucose, raises blood pressure, and sharpens attention. Cortisol isn't your enemy. It's your morning launch sequence.\n\nSo why does this hormone have such a terrible reputation? Because the same currency that funds a great morning, a strong workout, or a clutch presentation becomes toxic when you spend it **all day, every day** — and modern life is engineered to make you do exactly that.\n\nIn this lesson you'll learn cortisol's daily rhythm, the real difference between helpful and harmful stress, why 'adrenal fatigue' isn't what influencers claim, and the evidence-backed moves that put you back in charge of the budget.",
