            content: "Bring it all together:\n\n• Cortisol runs on a **diurnal wave** — peaking ~30 minutes after waking (the cortisol awakening response), bottoming out near midnight. The wave IS health; the plateau is the disease.\n• The **HPA axis** turns perceived threats into cortisol — and can't tell emails from emergencies. Recovery, not zero stress, is the goal.\n• **Chronic elevation** sends four compounding bills: visceral belly fat, elevated glucose via gluconeogenesis, broken sleep, and suppressed immunity — and each feeds your insulin resistance from last lesson.\n• **'Adrenal fatigue' is a myth** (Cadegiani 2016, 58 studies) — but **HPA dysregulation is real**, and real, testable conditions can hide behind the same symptoms.\n• The **five regulators** — moderate exercise, consistent sleep, breathwork, social connection, and work breaks — are not soft advice. They are measurable endocrine interventions.\n\nThe reframe worth keeping: cortisol is a currency. Spent in waves — a hard workout, a big presentation, a cold morning walk — it buys focus, energy, and growth. Spent continuously, it buys belly fat, bad nights, and every passing cold. You can't opt out of the currency. You CAN control the spending pattern.\n\n**Next lesson**: the gland cortisol loves to bully — your **thyroid**, the metabolic thermostat, and the lab tests that actually catch its problems.",
