            content: "There's a butterfly-shaped gland at the base of your throat, about the size of two thumbs, and it decides how fast every single cell in your body burns energy. Your heart rate, your body temperature, how quickly you think, how fast your hair grows — all of it runs at the speed your thyroid sets.\n\nHere's the unsettling part: roughly **5% of US adults** have an underactive thyroid, and a large share of them don't know it. The symptoms — fatigue, feeling cold, stubborn weight gain, brain fog — are so ordinary that people blame themselves. They think they're just getting older, or lazy, or depressed.\n\nBy the end of this lesson, you'll understand how the thermostat works, why it breaks, which blood tests actually reveal the problem, and how to have a smarter conversation with your doctor about it.",
