            title: "The Takeaway: Respect the Thermostat",
            content: "Let's lock in what you now know that most people don't:\n\n• Your thyroid sets the **metabolic speed of every cell**, and about **5% of US adults** — women 5-8x more often — run slow, many without knowing\n• **T4 is storage, T3 is active**, and the conversion between them happens mostly outside the thyroid — which is why one number can't tell the whole story\n• **TSH moves opposite to thyroid function**: high TSH = the pituitary shouting at an underperforming gland\n• **Hashimoto's autoimmunity** is the most common US cause, detectable early through TPO antibodies\n• **Subclinical hypothyroidism** is a genuine gray zone — the TRUST trial showed treatment isn't automatic, and honest medicine weighs symptoms, antibodies, and trajectory\n• The **symptom cluster** — fatigue, cold, weight, hair, fog — gets misfiled as aging or depression constantly. The pattern, not any one symptom, is the signal.\n\nYou can't feel your TSH. But you can notice patterns, ask for the right tests, keep your numbers, and work with a clinician who treats you — not just your lab sheet. That's what respecting the thermostat looks like.",
