            type: "application",
            title: "Recruit Your Hormones: This Week's Playbook",
            content: "**Five moves that shift the actual signals:**\n\n1. **Front-load protein** — aim for 25-30g at breakfast (eggs, Greek yogurt, leftover chicken). Protein is the strongest PYY/GLP-1 trigger, and a protein-rich morning measurably blunts evening snacking for many people.\n\n2. **Add fiber to your two biggest meals** — beans, vegetables, oats, berries. Fiber stretches the satiety-hormone release window instead of the 20-minute spike-and-crash of refined carbs.\n\n3. **Protect 7+ hours of sleep this week** — you now know two short nights move ghrelin +28% and leptin −18%. Treat your bedtime like an appetite medication schedule, because it is one.\n\n4. **Slow the first ten minutes of meals** — satiety hormones need time to release and reach the brain. Eating fast outruns the chorus; you finish before the \"enough\" votes arrive.\n\n5. **Retire the willpower story** — next time the 9:40 p.m. pull hits, name it: \"That's ghrelin, probably amplified by my short night.\" Naming the mechanism doesn't magically dissolve hunger, but it replaces shame with strategy — and strategy is what actually changes behavior.",
