            content: "Quick question: what do your bone density, your heart's arteries, your insulin sensitivity, your memory, and your skin's collagen all have in common?\n\nThey're all maintained, in part, by **estrogen** — a hormone most people file under \"reproduction\" and forget. Its partner **progesterone** gets even less credit, dismissed as \"the pregnancy hormone\" when it's also quietly shaping sleep, mood, and brain function.\n\nThis blind spot has real costs. Roughly **1 in 10 women** has PCOS — most undiagnosed for years. Another **1 in 10** has endometriosis — with an average diagnostic delay of about **seven years**. That's a decade of women being told their pain is normal, their symptoms are stress, their labs are \"fine.\"\n\nWhether you have these hormones or love someone who does, this lesson gives you the full map: what estrogen and progesterone actually do body-wide, what a normal cycle looks like, and how to spot the two conditions that hide in plain sight.",
