            type: "visual",
            title: "The Monthly Cycle: Four Phases, One Conversation",
            content: "A typical cycle runs **21-35 days** (28 is an average, not a rule). It's a four-phase hormonal conversation:\n\n**Menstrual (days ~1-5)**: both hormones low — the lining sheds. **Follicular (to ~day 13)**: FSH recruits follicles; rising estrogen rebuilds the lining and often lifts energy and mood. **Ovulation (~day 14)**: an LH surge releases the egg. **Luteal (~days 15-28)**: the corpus luteum pumps out progesterone; if no pregnancy, both hormones crash and the cycle restarts.\n\nThat late-luteal crash is the biology behind PMS week. It isn't imagined — it's withdrawal from two powerful neuroactive hormones at once.",
