            content: "Quick quiz: which hormone builds women's bones, drives women's libido, and circulates in every woman's bloodstream right now?\n\n**Testosterone.** Yes, really. Women don't just have it — before menopause, a woman's ovaries and adrenal glands make **more testosterone than estrogen** by weight most days of the month. It just gets far less press.\n\nMeanwhile, on the men's side, a billion-dollar 'Low T' industry wants every tired 45-year-old to believe his testosterone has fallen off a cliff and only a prescription — or a suspicious supplement — can save him.\n\nThe truth is more interesting than the marketing. In this lesson you'll learn what testosterone actually does in both sexes, what the real decline curve looks like (spoiler: it's a gentle slope, not a cliff), what a landmark 2023 trial of 5,246 men revealed about safety, and the free, evidence-backed levers that actually move your levels — starting tonight.",
