            content: "There's a good chance you — or someone in your house — has a bottle of melatonin in the medicine cabinet, used like a natural sleeping pill: can't sleep, take more.\n\nHere's the twist: **melatonin isn't a sedative at all.** It doesn't knock you out the way a sleeping pill does. It's a *signal* — your brain's way of announcing 'darkness has arrived; night operations may begin.' Using it like a knockout drug is like honking your horn to make traffic move: wrong tool, wrong mechanism.\n\nAnd melatonin is just the opening act of your body's night shift. While you sleep, an entire hormonal crew clocks in — including a **growth hormone surge in the first hours of deep sleep** that handles tissue repair, muscle recovery, and metabolic housekeeping.\n\nIn this lesson you'll learn how the darkness signal actually works, why your phone sabotages it, what the honest science says about melatonin supplements (dose and timing will surprise you), and the single free habit — involving your morning, not your night — that anchors your entire hormonal day.",
