            content: "Step back and look at what these three messengers have in common: **every one of them responds to what you do**.\n\n• **Dopamine** — you cannot delete the wanting system, but you can control its cues: fewer slot-machine triggers, more effort-then-reward loops (exercise, learning, building things) that pay dopamine the sustainable way\n• **Oxytocin** — released on demand by touch, trust, and time with people you care about\n• **Serotonin** — supported by daylight, movement, and the food you send to the gut that makes 90% of it\n\nNotice that the interventions overlap: a morning walk with a friend touches all three systems at once — plus the cortisol rhythm and melatonin timing you learned about earlier in this book. That overlap is not a coincidence. It is the thesis of this entire book, and the final lesson will make it explicit.\n\nBut first, one more practical stop. You have heard 'get your hormones checked.' Which tests actually mean something? Which are marketing? Next lesson: **how to read your hormone labs** — what to order, when to draw it, and what 'normal' really means.",
