            title: "'Your Labs Are Normal.' Then Why Do You Feel Awful?",
            content: "It is one of the most common — and most frustrating — sentences in medicine: *'Everything came back normal.'* You are exhausted, foggy, gaining weight, sleeping badly. And the paper says you are fine.\n\nSometimes you really are fine. But often the problem is different: **the wrong test was ordered, drawn at the wrong time, or read against the wrong question**. A TSH alone can miss a struggling thyroid. A random cortisol is nearly meaningless. A single testosterone draw can misdiagnose a healthy man. A 'normal' FSH cannot rule out perimenopause.\n\nThis lesson is your field guide to hormone testing: **which panels match which symptoms**, why timing changes everything, the difference between 'normal' and 'optimal,' the red flags that deserve an endocrinologist — and the expensive mail-order hormone kits you should skip entirely.\n\nYou will leave knowing how to walk into an appointment prepared, ask precise questions, and read your own results with clear eyes. Not medical advice — a smarter conversation with the person who gives it.",
